#142 (shapes) and #82 (pictures) can't be moved or resized in v0.3.0/v0.4.0. Both are fixed on main by #46, but its tests only use text boxes. This adds regression tests for the other objects so the fix stays fixed.

`click_resize_and_drag` in `crates/engine/src/cmd/objects.rs` follows the editor's own path:
- `layout.object_at` finds the object under a click at its centre;
- `select.range` over its character selects it;
- `arrange.bounds` with width/height resizes it and it stays inline;
- `arrange.bounds` with page/x/y floats it with Square wrap exactly where dropped, still selected;
- `arrange.nudge` moves it; surrounding text is untouched; undo restores the previous position.

Run for shapes (`rectangle`, `ellipse`, `star`, `arrow`) and for a picture.

Test only, no behaviour change. New tests pass, fmt and clippy pass. On my machine (Linux) a few existing tests in `wordcraft-layout` (`fragmented_hidden_text_…`, `tests_bidi::…`) and `wordcraft-pdf` (`field_results_are_extractable_text`) fail; they're in crates this PR doesn't touch and look font/environment-dependent.

Refs #142, #82

